# Twitch application client IDs — from https://dev.twitch.tv/console/apps
# Public by design (implicit OAuth has no secret); safe to commit in .env.
#
# Twitch matches the redirect URI byte-for-byte against the URLs registered on
# the app, so dev and prod normally use SEPARATE apps. The app is chosen by
# hostname at runtime: localhost -> _CLIENT_ID, anything else -> _CLIENT_ID_PROD
# (falling back to _CLIENT_ID if PROD is unset).
#
#   DEV  app's OAuth Redirect URLs must contain: http://localhost:5173
#   PROD app's OAuth Redirect URLs must contain: https://<your-domain>
#
# No trailing slash. The app logs the exact URI it sends to the console on load.
# Without these, chat still works — anonymous and read-only.
VITE_TWITCH_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_TWITCH_CLIENT_ID_PROD=
